# CKA Drill: JSONPath Speed & Output Formatting (`jsonpath`)

Master rapid resource queries and custom formatting under exam time limits using `-o jsonpath` and `--sort-by`.

## Exam Importance & Principles

- **Exam Domain**: Troubleshooting (30%) / Workloads & Scheduling (15%).
- **Frequency**: Often paired with tasks like: *"Extract all node internal IPs and save to /opt/nodes.txt"* or *"Find the pod with highest restarts"*.
- **Syntax Cheatsheet**:
  - Root element: `$` or `{}`
  - List iterator: `{.items[*]...}`
  - Specific item: `{.items[0]...}`
  - Wildcard all elements: `[*]`
  - Field accessor: `.metadata.name`
  - Filter query: `[?(@.type=="InternalIP")].address`
  - Newlines: `{"\n"}`
  - Custom column syntax alternative: `-o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,IP:.status.podIP`
  - Sorting: `--sort-by=.status.containerStatuses[0].restartCount` or `--sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp`

---

## High-Frequency Query Patterns

### 1. Extract Node Names and Internal IPs

```bash
kubectl get nodes -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{"\t"}{.status.addresses[?(@.type=="InternalIP")].address}{"\n"}{end}'
```

### 2. Extract Container Images of all Pods in a Namespace

```bash
kubectl get pods -n kube-system -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{"\t"}{.spec.containers[*].image}{"\n"}{end}'
```

### 3. Sort Pods by Restart Count

```bash
kubectl get pods -A --sort-by='.status.containerStatuses[0].restartCount'
```

### 4. Extract Pod Names in Status Running

```bash
kubectl get pods -o jsonpath='{.items[?(@.status.phase=="Running")].metadata.name}'
```

### 5. Extract PersistentVolume Names and Capacity

```bash
kubectl get pv -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{"\t"}{.spec.capacity.storage}{"\n"}{end}'
```

